It’s possible to access on the CAN bus by the diagnostic socket
also known as EOBD connector.
This connector usually is fitted on the driver side of the vehicle
between driver door and steering wheel.
The features of this connector are:
- it has16 pin;
- the pin 6 and 14 are reserved for EOBD CAN;
- the pin 4 and 5 are reserved for ground;
- the pin 16 is reserved for Power supply (+12V);
- the other pin are configurable from vendor.
